 "about": "FLOPs per contracted quartet of each of milestone 12's 21 HGP classes, x K^4 + y K^2 + z, from src/felizjueves/hgp/cost.py (#276), which reads the VRR DAG (hgp.vrr, #273) and the bra-first HRR DAG (hgp.hrr, #274), never the lowered IR. AN ENGINEERING INSTRUMENT CALIBRATED AGAINST NOTHING: [Fock] publishes no FLOP table, so there is no floor, no ratchet and no published comparison. Convention: one +, -, *, / is one FLOP (no FMA); an integer coefficient of +-1 and a sign cost nothing; a VRR node costs one multiply per term (two when |mult| > 1) plus n - 1 adds, the terms of eqs 25-26 as hgp.vrr.reduce lists them; an HRR node one multiply and one add; transcendentals (boys, rsqrt per quartet; exp per primitive pair) are named under 'transcendentals', not counted. x (K^4): quartet geometry, one seed multiply per Boys leaf, every VRR step, one add per boundary value accumulated; y (K^2): the bra pair's and the ket pair's geometry; z (K^0): every HRR step and the shell-pair separations. 'pruned' (the default, by decision: nothing downstream is ratcheted) counts the pruned VRR DAG; 'unpruned' the forward build; 'saving' is unpruned total - pruned total, reported, not asserted as a win. Eq 26's misprinted sign (fock/eq26-ket-vrr-sign, pending) moves no count: a sign costs nothing.",
